{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spectralLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = { _ in 1 }, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A is the weighted adjacency matrix: parallel edges add their weights, self-loops are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored, and a weight of 0 is no edge. The eigenvalues are sorted ascending with their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiplicity, so a graph with c components has c zero eigenvalues and its axes come from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eigenvectors of 0 when c > 1 (which ones is fixed by the solver, not specified). Each axis’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sign makes its first entry, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, whose magnitude is at least 10⁻⁴ of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"largest positive. Two vertices have y = 0, and one vertex is at the origin. The drawing is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not rescaled ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rescaled(scale:center:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps it to a common frame). A directed graph is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drawn through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dense: Householder tridiagonalization and the implicit QL iteration, O(n³) time and n²"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s, for graphs of up to a few thousand vertices."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Koren, “Drawing graphs by eigenvectors: theory and practice”, Computers & Mathematics with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Applications 49(11–12), 2005.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every weight is finite and not negative; "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"text":" after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":" QL iterations in all (30 n when nil), with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that count and the off-diagonal entry being reduced, relative to the largest entry of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"block. The iteration converges cubically, about two iterations per eigenvalue.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Throws"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"spectralLayout(weight:maxIterations:)","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/SpectralLayout.swift#L30","fileName":"SpectralLayout.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P0A7DrawingE14spectralLayout6weight13maxIterationsAD0C0Vy6VertexQzGSd5Edges_5IndexQZXE_SiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"spectralLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14G